      "en": "### Week 1: Hello, Teacher and Me\n\nChildren become familiar with teacher-led classroom interaction. The focus is responding to the teacher through looking, coming closer, waving, sitting nearby, accepting a simple object, or joining a short group routine.\n\n### Week 2: My Classroom and My Things\n\nChildren explore familiar classroom objects and personal items. The focus is touching, showing, giving, taking, putting objects in place, and beginning to understand that classroom objects have stable classroom homes.\n\n### Week 3: My Friends and Group Time\n\nChildren begin to notice classmates as part of a shared class group. The focus is sitting near peers, passing objects, taking turns with adult support, copying simple group actions, and joining short circle-time games.\n\n### Week 4: Classroom Routines and Clean-Up\n\nChildren practise repeated classroom routines such as clean-up, putting things back, lining up, moving between spaces, and finishing an activity. The focus is routine participation rather than independent mastery.",
