      "en": "This unit should not become an English vocabulary drilling unit. Classroom words are introduced through real routines, objects, teacher modelling, and repeated participation.\n\nThis unit should not repeat Unit Hello’s main emotional-settling function. Children may still need comfort and support, but the curriculum focus is now classroom participation rather than caregiver separation.\n\nThis unit should not require children to speak on demand. PG children may participate successfully through non-verbal responses, gesture imitation, object handling, movement, and adult-supported routine participation.\n\nThis unit should not overload children with too many classroom rules. Rules should be embedded in short, concrete routines such as sit on the mat, put the toy in the box, wait, line up, and all done.",
